<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What leaves the device, and what does not (API 31+; `backup_rules.xml` is the same
    decision for API 26–30).

    **Nothing goes to cloud backup.** People compute salaries, debts, rent and medical costs
    in a calculator — `docs/ANDROID_STANDARDS.md` §5 calls notepad documents the sensitive
    surface of this app, and says to exclude app data from cloud auto-backup unless the user
    opts into it. There is no opt-in yet, so the honest setting is none of it: no database,
    no settings, no cached rates.

    **Device transfer is allowed**, and the distinction is deliberate. A transfer copies the
    data directly to the new phone during setup, encrypted end to end and never sitting on
    Google's servers — it is the same device's data moving with the same person, which is
    what a user replacing a phone expects to happen to their notepad.

    `allowBackup` stays true because that is what makes device transfer possible at all.
    Turning it off would take both, to protect against neither.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="database" path="." />
        <include domain="file" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
